With regards to your message at 02:58 PM 7/1/01, Peter Watkinson. Where you 
stated:
>Hi,
>
>Thanks guys for the prompt reply.
>
>Maurice will you be selling Itanium systems? Also I see in your sig it says
>"Ask me about our New Alpha DDR Systems! " are these UP1500 stystems? can
>you tell us more?
Sure.
We have been testing and benchmarking the UP1500 for a few weeks now, and 
will be selling it once Samsung releases production products.
It is looking very good so far, with much better memory bandwidth than the 
UP1100, and roughly comparable to the UP2000.
It uses DDR ECC RAM, will hold up to 4GB, and currently the CPU is 800MHz 
3with 4MB of DDR cache.

A typical system will run $3,890, including:
  UP1500 Motherboard c/w 800MHz 4MBDDR cache CPU, ethernet, sound
17"  ATX  Tower, 2nd BB fan, 8 bay (6X+2i )
400W ATX Power (Zippy)
512MB PC2100 DDR ECC Reg DIMM
nVidia GeForce MX400 AGP 32MB
Onboard UDMA100 IDE Interface
Ethernet 10/100T on motherboard
Onboard SBPro compatible sound
IBM Deskstar 60GXP 7200rpm 40GB UDMA100 Hard Disk
Samsung 12XDVD / 48XCD ATAPI DVDROM
Panasonic 1.44MB, 3.5" floppy drive
Northern Linux (TM) 7.1 CDROM Set ( 6 CDs & Manual)
Logitech Deluxe Access keyboard PS/2 with wristrest
Logitech Mouseman  3 button mouse PS/2

If anyone would care for some of the results from popular benchmarks let me 
know by private email, and I will send them to you.

As for Itanium, if somebody wants us to build one, we will take your money.

If you want a recommendation of one, I will take a pass on that.
 From what I have seen so far the Itanium has precious little to make it 
desirable..

