I_realize_this_may_not be the correct forum,
however...

I just bought a PC164 mb and 533 21164 processor and
have an ATX case.  I intend to run linux on it. 
Before I hook it all up and apply power and fry
everything, I would like some help.  

Looking at the manual I noticed there isn't a jumper
to place the power switch lead for an ATX power
switch.  The ATX power connector fits.  Looking at the
PC164 power supply thread hints that I may want to get
a better supply the the 250 watt rated unit that is in
the case currently...

I am reasonably certain that once I have power to the
mother board and the bios boots and runs it's
diagnostics, that with the help of the manual I can
get my ram and crystals set up correctly.

Thanks-

Bryan Quick
