With regards to your message at 08:39 AM 7/7/01, Martin K. Petersen. Where 
you stated:
> >>>>> "Bryan" == quickman 99 <quickman_99@yahoo.com> writes:
>
>Bryan> Looking at the manual I noticed there isn't a jumper to place
>Bryan> the power switch lead for an ATX power switch.
>
>I had the same problem when I bought by PC164 many years ago.  I ended
>up looking at specs for the ATX connector and soldering a wire across
>two of the pins.
>
>If I remember correctly, I had to wire PS_ON to ground.  Can't check
>because my PC164 happens to be on the wrong continent right now.
>
>But check for yourself.  The ATX spec is here:
On an ATX supply, there is a green wire about in the middle of the row, 
with a black one immediately adjacent in the same row. These are the two 
that do the switching. Tie them together and you have a hard power switched 
supply.

