The sad situaltion is that Windows NT on the Alpha is dead, hence
development on milo also seems to have come to a dead halt and seems
to be no longer supported

Even in the longer term, SRM looks fated to go the same way as more
progress is made on LinuxBIOS.

API currently uses LinuxBIOs on it's CS20 range and from the few people
that I talked to it seems set to become the new trend. Though how portable
it
will be to older platforms seems a long way off.

For now I guess we'll have to scrape around and find working solutions for

the older kit and simply document it rather than support it in code.

