I have an  PC164SX  (I think that is SX164).
I have never been able to get anything but the
milo for SX164 that came with RH 5.X to work.
I think that is now biting me on my hindquarters.

When I boot RH 7.1 installation from the floppy
image using the arc console and milo it loads
the compressed image on the floppy and then
hangs after it says it is starting the kernel.  With
all of the problems people have had with SRM,
I just chose not to make the move.  I would like to
resolve the difficulty with later milo images:
how to get a newer one to compile without
a million error messages,  and:  how to 
get RH 7.1 installation from diskette boot/
CD-ROM  not to hang.  I have EIDE drive,
cabled to the board (Maxtor),  an ATI
Mach 64 PCI card,  and SB AWE64 sound card,
and a tulip driver ethernet card in it.  There is
nothing strange in this machine.  The machine
is currently running 2.2.19-7.0.8 and RH 7.0
without difficulty.

Thanks,
Bob McGwier




