Hi,

Eugene Chu wrote:

> Andrei A. Dergatchev wrote:
>
> >>Along the same theme, the driver I'm interested in is for an EMULEX
> >>LP8000 FibreChannel card.  EMULEX has a set of source code for a x86
> >>driver, but they saynothing about drivers for Alpha Linux.  I heard
> >>rumors of one, but I have yet to see it.
>
> >Hmm, just curious - is this card any better then Qlogic 2300, or even
> 2200?
>
> I guess it's about equivalent to the 2200 in fucntion and performance
> (both run SCSI and IP protocols and both run in FDX).  The big
> advantage with the LP8000 for me is that I'm currently using a bunch of
> them on my Suns, and I would like to keep them when I upgrade the Suns
> to Alphas.

Hey, good to hear somebody still calls it "an upgrade" even after Q killed
the king.

>
> I've been told that the QLOGIC 2XXX series are indeed supported on
> Alpha Linux, but I do not see such drivers at the QLOGIC site.  They
> seem to have 2 versions for i386 support.  Am I missing something?

Well, RH 7.0 (haven't tried 7.1 yet and all 6.2 isos I could find crash
on my SX) recognized and started to work with my 2200 without
me pushing a single key during installation. I guess the QLogic drivers
are in fact Alpha ready, but there is one in RH 7.0 anyhow. Moreover,
there is a QLogic driver by Matthew Jacob and yet other one by
Chris Loveland. All reportedly work under Alpha Linux or so I heard.

I also looked at Emulex cards but I recall someone told the don't
work under Alpha ...

>
> eyc
>

Regards,

Andrei




