On Fri, 20 Jul 2001, Andrei A. Dergatchev wrote:

> Well, RH 7.0 (haven't tried 7.1 yet and all 6.2 isos I could find crash
> on my SX) recognized and started to work with my 2200 without
> me pushing a single key during installation. I guess the QLogic drivers
> are in fact Alpha ready, but there is one in RH 7.0 anyhow. Moreover,
> there is a QLogic driver by Matthew Jacob and yet other one by
> Chris Loveland. All reportedly work under Alpha Linux or so I heard.

They work, from what I've seen, but they could be better.  64-bit support
is still mostly non-optimal (if it works at all, in some cases), and I've
seen a few unaligned traps being generated by one of those drivers as
well.  There's work being done on the drivers by Peter Petrakis, but he
hasn't had too much time to put into it.

C




