into the kernel.  It doesn't require any patches to the rest of the kernel.
I guess it would take someone to actually do that.

As far as getting my patch back to Qlogic, I probably have been too lazy.
At one point I talked to one of the engineers who was doing the development.
We had a pretty good relationship and I got him to make a few portability
changes.  He left the company and I was told it was best to go though
the general support email to talk to the developers.  I got lazy at that
point and never sent the changes to them.  

I should probably do it anyway.  I will put it on my list of things to do.
The problem is that the developers will have to change how they do things
to remember that the world is more than ia32 and ia64.

Craig






