Yes it is a SYMBIOS, but there is nothing connected to it. It is an out of
the box XP1000. No ad-on's, nothing. The graphics card is an ELSA Gloria
 ... Permedia2.

So, a detailed description:

667MHz, 1GB RAM, QLogic SCSI Controller with a HDD attached to it, ELSA
graphics card (Permedia2), tulip nic, IDE CDROM.

I always install in text mode. But what can I install if it doesn't even
boot? I'll try attach a serial cable to it, but to say it short, the well
known message, 'Ok, booting linux ...' is not reached.


On the other hand, I have installed Tru64 on the box and it rocks. It's
faster then any other alpha (with linux and Compaq compilers) we have
around here.

Thank you for your answers. I would be really happy if I could at least
boot linux on this box.

Regards,
Ionut

PS I have tried disconnecting the SYMBIOS controller ... to no avail.
PPS Could it be the RAM ? I have 4x256MB. Could I pull out a few of them ?

