Hi,

I am trying to serve an nis data base residing on a  Compaq tru64 machine
to my linux machines. I have setup one machine successfully, the same
setup on
another machine doesn't work. Both machines run RedHat 7.1 . Following is
some information to illustrate the setup and the problem.


-------------------------------

[root@rglinux2 ~]# ypcat -k passwd | grep reid
reid reid:xxx:662:20:Mark Reid,RG:/home/reid:/usr/local/bin/tcsh
---
[root@rglinux2 ~]# ypcat -k auto.home | grep reid
reid -rw,soft alpmjr:/u1/&
--
[root@rglinux2 ~]# ypcat -k auto.master
/home auto.home -rw,nosuid,hard,intr
/net -hosts     -rw,soft,intr,nosuid
/- auto.sys     -ro,soft,intr,nosuid
----
[root@rglinux2 ~]# su - reid
su: user reid does not exist

This is the problem, why is user reid not found?

-------

Also when I cd to /home/reid the directory exists, but when typing 
'ls -l' instead of user name the uid appears.

I will appreciate any suggestions.

Shoshana

srosenthal@cfa.harvard.edu





