Hi friends,

I want my system to beep when it is going rebooted / halted. I already put a
printf "\a" in my /etc/init.d/halt script. This works fine, but the problem is,
that I set the console to ttyS0 so all message will go to the serial line
including this last bell. Since I don't have a terminal attached to the machine
all the time I don't get the beep then.

My question: How can I access the internal speaker of the AS200.
Note: i commented the lines for the virtual consoles in /etc/inittab out. (I
get an error from init (id X respawning too fast ...)). So I just have a login
prompt at the serial line

